<title>AUSTRIA: Radex ups 1996 dividend to 15 ats, earnings rise.</title>
<headline>Radex ups 1996 dividend to 15 ats, earnings rise.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Final results for the business</p>
<p>year ending December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of schillings unless stated)</p>
<p>					 1996		  1995</p>
<p> Group sales		     21,005		21,691</p>
<p> Group earnings before	    911		   722</p>
<p>interest and tax</p>
<p> Group pre-tax			674		   577</p>
<p> Group net			    582		   467</p>
<p> Dividend (schillings)	     15		    14</p>
<p> Group EPS (schillings)	    36		    30</p>
<p>Fireproof/engineering division:</p>
<p> Total sales		     16,711		17,477</p>
<p>    Fireproof		    14,853		15,219</p>
<p>    Engineering		   1,858		 2,258</p>
<p> Total operating		    770		   565</p>
<p>    Fireproof			 782		   565</p>
<p>    Engineering		     (12)		    0</p>
<p> Total pre-tax			582		   483</p>
<p>    Fireproof			 632		   542</p>
<p>    Engineering		     (50)		  (59)</p>
<p>Insulation division:</p>
<p> Sales				4,333		 4,252</p>
<p> Operating			    163		   191</p>
<p> Pre-tax				140		   162</p>
<p>NOTE - Full company name is Radex-Heraklith Industriebeteiligungs AG. Radex said it had raised its stake in Germany's Didier-Werke AG to 57.6 percent at the start of the year.</p>
<p>NOTE - Radex said return on sales rose to 3.2 percent last year from 2.7 percent in 1995. The firm said it had come a significant step closer to its goal of a return on sales of five percent in 1998.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom, +43-1 531 12 254</p>
